               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, a 26-year-old male, admitted on 26/02/1998 with acute right iliac fossa pain, nausea, and low-grade fever. Clinical examination revealed marked tenderness at McBurney's point with rebound tenderness. Laboratory investigations confirmed leukocytosis, and abdominal ultrasound supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. The patient was resuscitated with intravenous fluids and commenced on broad-spectrum antibiotics. Following anaesthetic assessment, the patient underwent an uncomplicated open appendectomy on 27/02/1998. Histopathological examination confirmed acute appendicitis. Postoperative recovery was uneventful, with adequate pain management and wound care provided. The patient was discharged home on 28/02/1998 in good general condition. Please ensure follow-up wound inspection in approximately one week and review histology results when available. Should any concerns arise, please do not hesitate to contact us.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
